<title>FRANCE: Dassault slumps after delayed opening.</title>
<headline>Dassault slumps after delayed opening.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in planemaker Dassault Aviation were sharply lower on the Paris bourse on Monday after a delayed opening due to an imbalance in orders.</p>
<p>The stock was down 9.59 percent at 981 francs at 0905 GMT after opening 8.8 percent lower.</p>
<p>Dassault Aviation, which risks being nationalised if the privatisation of its merger partner Aerospatiale is scuppered, fell sharply last week after the Socialists won the first round of the parliamentary election, putting the privatisation of Aerospatiale in doubt.</p>
</text>
